.TH DKIM2-MILTER 8 "2026-11-03" "dkim2" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
dkim2\-milter \- DKIM2 Milter adapter for Postfix
.SH SYNOPSIS
.ad l
.nh
.in +4n
.ti -4n
\fBdkim2\-milter\fR serve \-\-config <absolute\-path>
.br
.ti -4n
\fBdkim2\-milter\fR validate \-\-config <absolute\-path>
.br
.ti -4n
\fBdkim2\-milter\fR probe \-\-config <absolute\-path>
.br
.ti -4n
\fBdkim2\-milter\fR \-\-version
.in -4n
.hy
.ad
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dkim2\-milter
connects an MTA that speaks the Milter protocol to
.BR dkim2d (8).
It collects the SMTP envelope and the message at end of message, sends them to
one configured daemon route, and applies the returned action: accept, insert
header fields at the top of the header block, temporarily fail, or reject.
It owns no DKIM2 protocol rules.
.PP
Each process runs exactly one mode, selected in its configuration:
.B inbound
verification,
.B originator
signing,
.B ordinary_transit
revision of forwarded mail, or
.B postfix_dsn
signing of bounces.
Run one instance per mode, each with its own Unix socket and capability.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Create the configured Unix socket and serve Milter sessions until SIGTERM or
SIGINT.
.TP
.B validate
Load the strict configuration and its route capability without opening a
socket or contacting the daemon.
It is silent on success; run it after every change.
.TP
.B probe
Reload the configuration and check that its socket exists, is a single\-link
Unix socket owned by the effective UID, and grants nothing to other users.
It neither opens a Milter session nor contacts the daemon.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIstring\fR
absolute path to the configuration document
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
help for dkim2\-milter
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
version for dkim2\-milter
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every stable configuration path may also be supplied through its single
declared environment name behind the
.B DKIM2_MILTER_
prefix.
A value set in both places is a configuration error.
Scalar values may contain
.B ${NAME}
placeholders, expanded before validation; a missing variable fails closed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, help output, or a clean shutdown.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration, startup, validation, probe, or runtime failure.
.TP
.B 2
Command shape or flag error.
.PP
Per message, the default
.B failure.mode: tempfail
answers local or daemon failure with
.B 451 4.7.1
and an explicit daemon rejection with
.BR "550 5.7.1" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dkim2/milter/<mode>.yaml
Configuration document for one instance, as used in the Postfix guide.
.TP
.I /etc/dkim2/milter/<mode>/capability
The 32\-byte route capability (mode 0400 or 0600) in a parent of exact mode
0500.
Never place it on a command line or in an environment value.
